{#-
Extractors:
  - ledger: AnchorExtractor("<LEDGER>", "</LEDGER>")
  - facts (when establish_facts): AnchorExtractor("<FACTS>", "</FACTS>")

Override example:
  {{ set_anchor_extractor("ledger", "<MY_TAG>", "</MY_TAG>") }}
-#}
{% if recent_lines %}
<|SECTION:RECENT LINES|>
{% for entry in recent_lines %}
{{ entry }}
{% endfor %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endif %}
<|SECTION:NEW LINE|>
{{ line }}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% for name, facts in absence.items() %}
<|SECTION:WHAT {{ name.upper() }} DOES NOT KNOW YET|>
{% for fact in facts %}
- [{{ fact.id }}] {{ fact.text }}
{% endfor %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endfor %}
{% if establish_facts and previous_facts -%}
<|SECTION:KNOWN FACTS|>
{% for fact in previous_facts %}
- [{{ fact.id }}] {{ fact.text }}
{% endfor %}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{% endif -%}
<|SECTION:TASK|>
{{ speaker }} just said the new line above, with {{ listeners }} present. For each listener, decide which of the facts they did not know yet the new line reveals to them. A fact counts as learned only when the line states it or makes it plain; a hint, a question, or a related fact does not count.

Answer with a JSON object inside the tags: one key per listener, the value the list of fact ids they learned. Leave a listener out when they learned nothing. Answer <LEDGER>{}</LEDGER> when nobody learned anything.

Example: <LEDGER>{"Mara": ["F12"], "Edwin": []}</LEDGER>
{% if establish_facts %}

Also extract the new facts established by the NEW LINE only. Recent lines and known facts are context, not additional material to extract. Preserve what {{ speaker }} says as attributed speech when it is a report or claim. Do not turn a claim into world truth. Do not repeat an already recorded fact; use supersedes only for a new fact that changes or replaces an earlier fact, never for an unchanged restatement.

{% include "fact-extraction-instructions.jinja2" %}

After </LEDGER>, return a second block:
<FACTS>
[{"text": "one self-contained statement, names spelled out, no pronouns", "importance": 2, "subjects": ["characters, items or places the fact is about"], "known_by": ["listeners who learned the fact"], "supersedes": null}]
</FACTS>
Choose importance 1, 2, or 3 using the rules above. Name only the listeners supplied above in known_by. Everyone present knows the attributed fact; known_by describes learning and does not restrict the audience. Reference only supplied known fact IDs in supersedes. Between 0 and 12 items. Return <FACTS>[]</FACTS> when the line establishes nothing worth keeping. Output both blocks, without another response or request.
{% endif -%}
<|CLOSE_SECTION|>
{{ set_prepared_response("<LEDGER>") }}
